From 9a908097c192a39d82293bd99ed3e032555762f4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bradent27-sketch <304192343+bradent27-sketch@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 10:13:52 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Retire v2_season_anchor, v2_anchor_s_refit,
 v2_expected_points_luck, v2_luck_te_refit, v2_luck_qb (code moves to
 data/retired_points_steps.py)

All five were SHIPPED, measured to help, and turned off 2026-11-02 because the stat recal plus v2_points_from_stat_line replace the
weeks 3-17 total (the `lean` harness arm, pfs without them, tied pfs: START identical at every position and stat). They are superseded,
not failed:
- v2_season_anchor (2026-10-06): final total shrunk toward the player's own to-date mean (RB 0.75, WR 0.69, TE 0.84); held-out RMSE
  better in all six year splits (-0.027 ALL). v2_anchor_s_refit (2026-10-28) weakened it (RB 0.88, WR 0.82, TE 1.0) and missed its bar on 2023.
- v2_expected_points_luck (2026-10-20): a WR/TE total pulled against how far earlier games ran ahead of nflverse expected points
  (-0.18 WR, -0.16 TE; START-ALL -0.0055, 4 of 4 seasons). v2_luck_te_refit (-0.33) and v2_luck_qb (-0.11, centered on the average QB's
  luck) refit it on 2026-10-28.
The functions, constants and factor selectors moved verbatim to data/retired_points_steps.py (re-exported from data.weekly_projections,
because about a dozen calibration scripts import them); the model loses the five flags, the two build steps, their explanation hooks and
the POST_CALIBRATION_FEATURES entries. Their unit tests moved to tests/test_retired_points_steps.py; the two build-level tests, which
needed the flags, went with them. Restore with git revert of this commit.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
